$abs(bold(a) times bold(b))$ is the area of the parallelogram formed by $bold(a)$ and $bold(b)$, so the triangle $O A B$ with $bold(a) = arrow(O A)$, $bold(b) = arrow(O B)$ has area $(1)/(2) abs(bold(a) times bold(b))$. Fixing $bold(a)$ and restricting to $bold(x) perp bold(a)$, the map $bold(x) mapsto bold(a) times bold(x)$ scales $bold(x)$ by $abs(bold(a))$ and rotates it by $(pi)/(2)$ within the plane orthogonal to $bold(a)$.
